//BUG="a call's explicit template arguments are never lowered"
//OUT="1 2"

// Not in FEEDBACK.md, and the other half of 09_tuples/11. That case covers a
// tuple type nested in a template argument of a *signature*, which is lowered
// because `lower_ast` walks every function's argument types. A tuple written
// at a call site is not: `Lowerer::lower_expression` handles
// `ASTExpressionKind::FunctionCall` with
//
//     call.arguments = self.lower_expressions(call.arguments);
//
// and leaves `call.template_arguments` alone. `StructInitialization` right
// above it does lower its template arguments, so the omission looks
// accidental. `MethodCall` has the same gap.
//
// So `Vec[i32, i32]()` and `make[i32, i32]()` abort the compiler on
// `unreachable!("ASTType::Tuple should be eliminated by lowerer")`, while the
// same vector spelled `v: Vec[i32, i32] = Vec()` compiles and runs.

fn main
    v = Vec[i32, i32]()
    v.push((1, 2))
    out "{v[0].0} {v[0].1}"
